rivative of the natural logarithm is the reciprocal function:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}x)=\\frac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nWe apply our formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\operatorname{ln}x) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}x) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186237851 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a71301e9-bc7f-53b9-900e-c3bd37f96b03" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating the Product of a Constant and the Natural Logarithm Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e1d6f3e-9053-5690-b000-66d554fc0b32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e}{2x}" :db/id 17592186236110} {:answer/id #uuid "3532faea-48d8-5741-aa13-a64cbba7d647" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{ex}" :db/id 17592186236153} {:answer/id #uuid "4e1aa2e2-8a76-5713-9b50-46a772b85443" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2e}{x}" :db/id 17592186236316} {:answer/id #uuid "a1648056-d8f0-59f6-985d-fcda1cb5175d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+\\frac{e}{x}" :db/id 17592186236828} {:answer/id #uuid "d8be5480-6829-5df9-a0e9-113723bfaa4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e+\\frac{2}{x}" :db/id 17592186237188}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e1aa2e2-8a76-5713-9b50-46a772b85443" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2e}{x}" :db/id 17592186236316} :answer-field/id #uuid "994834f1-4e9a-532e-b583-a55ce29002bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186237641}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "319b8cc3-c619-5308-8487-fad516398fb6" :question/math-academy-id "q-101600" :question/problem "Given that $y=2eln⁡x$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The derivative of the natural logarithm is the reciprocal function:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ln⁡x)=\\frac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nWe apply our formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2eln⁡x) \\\\  & =2e\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ln⁡x) \\\\  & =2e\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2e}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186237852 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a71301e9-bc7f-53b9-900e-c3bd37f96b03" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating the Product of a Constant and the Natural Logarithm Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5235b2d2-41a6-571c-8e01-a03aeb01451b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{9x}" :db/id 17592186236336} {:answer/id #uuid "7f36f138-72b0-5be3-99c0-4538ad3f84d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id 17592186236605} {:answer/id #uuid "a14212af-f2a6-570c-8589-28ef6e251469" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{x}" :db/id 17592186236826} {:answer/id #uuid "d3777975-3ec1-5d04-845f-b4ae29e575be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{x}" :db/id 17592186237153} {:answer/id #uuid "d511865a-f893-5e0e-83a5-afff6f3a9a90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x}{9}" :db/id 17592186237163}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a14212af-f2a6-570c-8589-28ef6e251469" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{x}" :db/id 17592186236826} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d97240d-1080-5a25-924c-3b346338aa89" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186237581}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "681375a5-0c42-5d37-8f3f-a0f73ddc205e" :question/math-academy-id "q-101604" :question/problem "Given that $y=-9ln⁡x$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The derivative of the natural logarithm is the reciprocal function:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ln⁡x)=\\frac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nWe apply our formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-9ln⁡x) \\\\  & =-9\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ln⁡x) \\\\  & =-9\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186297307 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a71301e9-bc7f-53b9-900e-c3bd37f96b03" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating the Product of a Constant and the Natural Logarithm Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87066e75-093e-5691-a45a-e1a86f0a53fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{x}" :db/id 17592186295992}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87066e75-093e-5691-a45a-e1a86f0a53fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{x}" :db/id 17592186295992} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc24bef9-c819-59a0-b467-817f630d6de4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186297151}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a09e33e6-12c2-544c-8fa4-02ef6f3be0de" :question/math-academy-id "q-308849" :question/problem "Given that $y=8ln⁡x$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The derivative of the natural logarithm is the reciprocal function:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ln⁡x)=\\frac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nWe apply our formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(8ln⁡x) \\\\  & =8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ln⁡x) \\\\  & =8\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/i